ith over  the last three years during covet and I  feel like they're safe and then I  connect the two my wife is also involved  she's the social worker so she's very  good at making the connection  and a lot of them go and see the doctor  a lot most of the time it's Secret in  secrecy they have to actually say  certain words and sentences to be able  to see that that doctor and I've learned  those two are from the doctors that I'm  they're my colleagues in Iran like they  have to say Mr whatever referred me to  you for this it might be like a weight  loss clinic that are actually taking out  sutures or they're taking out pallets so  the situation is very convoluted  um but I guess I just you know the  easiest example I can give you is like  that  so and maybe you can talk a little bit  about the most common injuries you're  seeing the most common are  um wounds from pellets  um they can be from bird shots majority  are bird shots because they're multiple  anywhere from 20 pellets to 50 to 100  and now I'm seeing injuries with a paint  gun where the actual bullet is metal  it's not from a pinch so I'm staying I'm  seeing a larger wound with necrotic  surrounding they don't penetrate inside  the body but again if they don't take  care of that wound it can become  infected and they can be septic but the  pellets are actually penetrating where  they can severe arteries and it can  cause damage to the nerves if they're in  a joint they have to be operated on so  my job is kind of triaging like who  really needs to go see an orthopedic  surgeon who really needs to go to the ER  how dangerous the these gunshot wounds  are I'm also seeing a lot of second and  third degree burns from electrical  batons that they're using a lot of these  Burns need medical attention like IV  antibiotics IV fluids large bruises  throughout their body from fighting with  the police or falling down while they're  running away these can turn into  compartment syndrome plantar fasciae  necrotizing fasciitis these are very  life-threatening conditions where  sometimes I get an image three days  later I get a follow-up image that I say  oh no you have to go see a surgeon right  now let me find you one but the  conditions where they're operating on  these individuals are sub-optimal  they're not the normal conditions you  would see in in our countries here how  is the supply situation in in hospitals  in Iran I'm glad you asked that it's the  first time I've been asked that question  it's uh very scarce  um medication especially antibiotics  because of this situation a lot of  people are getting shot but so they have  to take prophylactic antibiotics I just  found out the other day that many  pharmacies do not have enough supplies  to give to people so a lot of people are  just using maybe home remedies or  putting honey in their wounds for  healing  um and in terms of whether they need  surgical procedures a lot of them are  using tweezers that they're disinfecting  over the candle fire and just using that  they're not using actual surgical  instruments if they end up going to a  clinic that's private and safe they may  they will get decent care of their  wounds but again my biggest fear is the  low supply of antibiotics and also  tetanus vaccine because a lot of these  individuals would need tetanus boosters  and they're running low on that too  you've been offering medical advice  online now for weeks is the situation  getting worse how would you describe it  I think it's as bad as it was three  weeks ago I continuously get questions  about injuries I'm not seeing a decrease  in the number of number of SOS messages  that I get on my Instagram  that's why I'm kind of reaching out to  the community outside of Iran for for  help and I I do feel hopeless at some  points because I cannot keep up with all  these messages how many messages do you  get doctor  um I extrapolated based on an hourly  message close to 300 to 500 messages a  day every 24 hours what is your main  Channel you you get these images  it's Instagram my page  um Dr K which um I I started the page  three years ago when covet started so it  gained a significant popularity in Iran  I think it has become their number  source of medical information right now  what about uh internet censorship is it  difficult uh for your patients in Iran  to contact you via Instagram and other  social media platforms uh yeah there's  times where I don't receive any messages  and I know there's some sort of  censorship or block going on on the  internet sometimes there's a delay where  somebody is at a friend's house bleeding  out of their leg and they're waiting to  send that message to me uh just imagine  that you're responsible for helping  somebody many many thousands of miles  away and you're not even able to receive  their message like they're sending an  image of somebody I had a patient that  got shot in the eye but the mess the  picture was not coming to me because how  slow the internet was  so even from like a technological  standpoint making the connection of  trying to get help is getting more  difficult so you know they're just it's  just getting very hard for them to take  care of themselves that brings me to my  question doctor what could the  International Community uh do to help  people in Iran protesters in Iran I feel  hopeless you know I unless these  something happens that you know they're  able to go get go to the hospital go see  their doctors I feel like you know  um I see no light down the tunnel to be  honest with you but I do have a lot of  other doctors a lot of nurses inside  Iran outside of Iran all trying to help  and that's really what gets me going you  know the unity that Iranian people have  to help each other what keeps them going  I don't know I talk I talk to a lot of  my Iranian people and they feel like  this time it's different it there is a  and uh there's a Unity you know in all  of Iran and outside of Iran I don't know  if um if you 